cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "NLMFSP: Nonlocal Mean Field Schrödinger Bridge with Learned Interactions"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the paper it accompanies, given under
  preferred-citation below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Daisuke
    family-names: Inoue
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2877-3438"
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics, Imperial College London"
  - given-names: Dante
    family-names: Kalise
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2327-1957"
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics, Imperial College London"
  - given-names: Mathieu
    family-names: Laurière
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4380-1399"
    affiliation: "NYU-ECNU Institute of Mathematical Sciences, NYU Shanghai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/inody/nlmfsp"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a four-stage alternating scheme that solves
  mean-field Schrödinger bridge problems with nonlocal interactions by replacing
  the pairwise interaction sums with neural surrogates, reducing the per-step
  cost from quadratic to linear in the population size.
keywords:
  - Schrödinger bridge
  - mean-field control
  - forward-backward stochastic differential equations
  - neural surrogates
  - nonlocal interactions
license: Apache-2.0

